the BMW motorrad days is the biggest BMW  motorcycle festival in the world for  three days the two withers take center  stage in the southern german town of  garmisch-partenkirchen  is the 13th time the event has been  staged and it's grown in popularity far  beyond Germany's borders this year  40,000 visitors from 40 countries came  to pay tribute to Beamer bikes  it was a laid-back friendly and very  informal atmosphere  among the many bikes on show were these  handcrafted one offs from the Berlin  firm urban motor their classic BMW s are  transformed into the clients  custom-built dream machines  nite chef it's all about passion  according to urban motors painted  diamond bag for mechanics old  motorcycles and old boxer engines so  they have the idea of making unique  models BMW is building block principle  means they can turn them into anything  the firm mainly works with bikes from  the 1970s and 80s there are many  similarities the engines and frames are  the same so they can be changed in any  way thinkable it could be a flat tracker  our cafe racer or a crossover model a  roadster whatever the customer wants so  I guess I'm going said come and sell as  much the bikes don't just look great  they also pack some real power a bmd  classic boxer sprint was put through its  paces in an eight mile drag race  sorry mom is equal in other yes via  nematode a plastic boxes it's a videsh  bus this is the fun part for Peter Donna  bag it's all about going head to head  and putting on a show he says it's not  about winning it's about letting your  bikes roar and leaving some rubber on  the road that's what it's about doesn't  see how it's up deployed  the urban motor team are certainly  enjoying the knockout competition a huge  adrenaline rush you open the throttle  and people love it this year also marks  a special anniversary the first BMW  motorcycle hit the market 90 years ago  some of the Marquis milestone machines  were out on display here like this are  23 from the very first production series  only around 3000 were built for this are  69 s with a top speed of 175 kilometers  an hour it was the fastest German  motorbike back in 1967  the f650 went into production in 1993 it  was BMWs most successful motorbike well  into the 2000s and there are no shortage  of future BMW fans in Germany the moto  rod days give junior bikers a chance to  put their motocross skills on show  you
 

